Author: Félicien Akohoue [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Félicien Akohoue <akohoue.f@gmail.com>
Description: Provides auditable multi-trait selection-index tools for plant
    breeding programs. The desired-gain selection index (DGSI) searches for
    coefficients whose realised response approaches breeder-defined targets
    and reports optimisation stability across independent searches.
    The quadratic genomic selection index (QGSI) scores genomic estimated
    breeding values with explicit linear economic weights and a validated
    symmetric matrix of squared and cross-product economic weights, following
    Ceron-Rojas et al. (2026) <doi:10.1038/s41467-026-69890-3>. It estimates or
    accepts the genomic covariance matrix and reports the model-based index
    mean, variance, selection response, expected gains, and, when true genetic
    covariance is available in simulation, accuracy and prediction error.
    Results also include covariance provenance, automatic DGSI replicate
    selection, convergence and stability diagnostics, eligibility decisions,
    rankings, and candidate-specific score contributions.
